                  border: 1px solid rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.28) !important;
                  border-radius: var(--ha-card-border-radius, 20px) !important;
                  {# EN | THE ONE TEXT FIELD IN THIS CONSOLE.
                     EN | An input_text row is rendered by Home Assistant as
                     EN | `ha-input` > `wa-input` (Web Awesome), and the fill
                     EN | of that box comes from --ha-color-form-background,
                     EN | whose default is LIGHT. On this dark console that is
                     EN | a white box holding a pale cyan label and a white
                     EN | value — both unreadable. Measured on the live
                     EN | console: rgb(243,243,243) fill, rgb(255,255,255)
                     EN | text.
                     EN | Note it is NOT the mdc-text-field-* / input-* names
